/*!
\mainpage

Welcome to the user manual for the CrysPy Kernel, the open-source core of the extensible multiscale crystal plasticity framework CrysPy. It contains the computational kernel of the framework, wrapped in a minimalistic command line interface. CrysPy Kernel is aimed at expert users who require full control of their crystal plasticity simulations and/or wish to set up automated workflows. Familiarity with the subject matter and working with the CLI are expected.

If you are looking for a more convenient, albeit less customizable user-experience, you may be interested in purchasing the full CrysPy framework, which includes a much more elaborate, web-based graphical user interface. Contact the <a href="https://numa.cs.kuleuven.be/">KU Leuven NUMA research group</a> for more information.

Contents
---------------
- \ref page_conventions summarizes the notation conventions in this manual.
- \ref page_cryspy_usage outlines the CrysPy workflow.
- \ref page_cryspy_format specify the format used for CrysPy inputs and outputs.
- \ref page_cryspy_specification details the configuration settings and outputs for CrysPy simulations.
- \ref page_theory introduces the foundations of the CrysPy framework and the ALAMEL crystal plasticity model, which was the original catalyst for developing this framework.
*/
